/**
	The volume of the voice, from -100 (silent) to 0 (loudest), as in BGT, with -50 being the middle of the engine's range.
	float tts_voice::volume;
	## Remarks:
		Values outside the range are clamped to it. Until it is assigned, it reports the volume the engine starts with, which may not be 0; see volume_set for what that is on each platform. With Speech Dispatcher on Linux, which uses its own configuration, it reports 0 until assigned, and assigning it doesn't change the speech. This is the property form of set_volume and get_volume.
*/

// Example:
void main() {
	tts_voice v;
	v.volume = -20;
	v.speak_wait("This is spoken a little more quietly, at a volume of " + v.volume + ".");
}
